      "text": "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\nIf \n\ud835\udc50\n=\n\ud835\udf06\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n3\n\ud835\udc4f\n, then \n\ud835\udf06\n=\n \n.\n\nCORRECT\nPreview only\nSolution:\n\nAnswer 1 \u00b7 correct value:\n\n\u2212\n1\n\nFirst trace \n3\n\ud835\udc4f\n from the common origin \n\ud835\udc42\n to a point \n\ud835\udc43\n: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from \n\ud835\udc43\n to the endpoint \n\ud835\udc36\n must be the unknown multiple of \n\ud835\udc4e\n.\n\nFollowing the grid direction of \n\ud835\udc4e\n takes \n4\n steps, while the parallel path \n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n has \n4\n steps. Their length ratio is \n4\n4\n=\n1\n. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to \n\ud835\udc4e\n, so\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n=\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n.\nAdding the path vectors gives\n\ud835\udc50\n\t\n=\n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc43\n\u2192\n+\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n\n\t\n=\n3\n\ud835\udc4f\n+\n(\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n)\n\n\t\n=\n\u2212\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n3\n\ud835\udc4f\n.\nBecause \n\ud835\udc4e\n and \n\ud835\udc4f\n are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with \n\ud835\udc50\n=\n\ud835\udf06\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n3\n\ud835\udc4f\n gives \n\ud835\udf06\n=\n\u2212\n1\n. The minus sign records the reversed direction.\n\nBack to study \u2192",
